Subject: [PATCH 04/18] B70: open-ended research with explicit wiki-save
 wording stays on the direct-save route

An explicit wiki-save request now keeps product-shaped and multi-entity
questions ("best options around $1000", "recommend") on the guarded
generic route, which saves the verified answer directly, instead of the
approval-based product route. An explicit controller product marker
still selects the product route, travel requests keep the travel route,
and requests without save wording route as before.

Open-ended requests (best, options, budget, recommend and so on, without
an explicit 2-3 way comparison) get a larger bounded budget of 5 searches
and 3 extract calls, plus a note to identify candidates and always include
any option the operator names. The controller then waits once for at
least 4 extracted pages before sealing the receipt; after one deferral it
seals with what it has. Other requests keep 3 searches and 2 extract
calls. The receipt helper's upper bounds were raised to match, outside
this repository. User-authorized on 2026-09-27.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
